    "scope": "Explicit idempotent detach/drain close on the existing continuation only; not a new bridge or settlement owner.",
    "behavior": [
      "Close synchronously fences this continuation and returns one cached native Promise.",
      "An idle close detaches only the continuation's explicit SDK/transport references.",
      "A queued resume is refused before its borrowed SDK capability is invoked.",
      "An already invoked resume is observed until its native Promise settles. Close waits for this owned run's finally path, without cancellation or rollback.",
      "A late success is not returned as a continuation success. Underlying SUCCEEDED/ACKNOWLEDGED facts and prior publication uncertainty remain separately visible.",
      "Returning this continuation's own close Promise is refused instead of creating a direct receipt dependency deadlock.",
      "Permanent hash/continuation claims, consumed first authority and observer budgets are never reset or reclaimed."
    ],
    "snapshotAdditions": [
      "closed",
      "closeOutcome",
      "settlementState"
    ],
    "defaultBoundary": "No active buyer/server/CLI cutover, new operational helper or external dependency. Existing default-role methods, verifier/first-settlement/observer ownership and wire receipt checks are retained.",
    "retentionBoundary": "DETACHED means five explicit continuation reference variables are null. The bridge/owner still retains original serialized bindings, hash claims and trusted role capabilities; other references are not revoked. No GC, erasure or measured memory reclamation is claimed.",
    "lifetimeBoundary": "A borrowed operation that never settles can keep close pending indefinitely. This is not bridge/owner shutdown, revocation, a hard timeout, lifetime/cancellation/native-cleanup or OS/network-sandbox guarantee; indirect cycles remain a trusted-capability limitation."
